  "changes": [
    "Tracks the last actually acknowledged temporary lease override for its real session identity.",
    "If a successor acquisition is invalidated before dispatch while an earlier temporary lease remains installed, the failed successor cleanup clears the still-owned predecessor rather than exposing a stable capture with stale temporary server state.",
    "Acknowledged restore and explicit ownerless writes retire the temporary-lease record after their server write; queued cleanup remains guarded by operation generation and retained session transport.",
    "Adds one host control: acquire temporary lease A, queue successor B, invalidate before B dispatch, verify cleanup sends null and no writable receipt is issued."
  ],
  "baseline_scope": "Same four primary baseline IDs and partial AI validation-generation boundary as V7/V6; no additional baseline units claimed. Four new race controls total relative to V8 baseline (two from the original V5 patch, one queued ownerless-clear control in V7, one undispatched-successor cleanup control in V8). Existing selector partition assignment unchanged.",
